! v1.20.0 CROSS-CHECK: two initial guesses, one system.
!
! CHF2O is an open-shell radical on which %initial_guess sad --
! the DEFAULT for open shells -- converges to a solution 3.3 mHa
! ABOVE the one hcore finds, after 144 iterations, five MOM
! reorderings and an automatic level shift.  The hcore result
! agrees with ORCA to 3.7e-9 Ha; the sad result is off by 3.3e-3.
! Spin contamination is nearly identical (0.7570 vs 0.7574), so
! these are two orbital occupations of the same spin state, not
! two spin states.
!
! Two guesses of the same SCF must reach the same minimum.  This
! pair needs no external reference to detect that they do not,
! which is why it belongs in the suite rather than in a table.
%method  HF
%basis   cc-pVDZ
%job     energy
%charge  0
%mult    2
%spherical
%initial_guess hcore
%scf_etol 1e-10
%scf_ptol 1e-8
%scf_diis_etol 1e-7
%geom angstrom
O       0.0000000000      0.0000000000      0.0000000000
C       0.0000000000      0.0000000000      1.5000000000
H       1.0306152474      0.0000000000      1.8548692884
F      -0.6240422599      1.0808729002      1.9297499639
F      -0.6240422599     -1.0808729002      1.9297499639
*end
